{
  "plugin": "hockey-scoreboard",
  "_comment": "Hockey keeps one manager per league and mode as a plain attribute -- nhl_live, ncaa_mens_recent and so on -- and only builds them when that league's enabled flag is set, so the config below turns the NHL on. Every mode's display() returns early unless games_list is populated, and the live path also reads live_games and active_celebration. display_mode picks which of the nine screens is drawn. The card reads home_logo_path/away_logo_path off the game dict as Path objects, and period_text is what hockey.py's extractor builds for that state (P1-P3, OT1, Final, Final/OT). Live games also carry away_shots/home_shots and power_play, hockey's own fields. Teams, scores and records are invented. There is deliberately no power-play image: show_powerplay is resolved into the manager config and power_play is extracted onto the game dict, but nothing in the plugin or the core ever draws either, so no config produces a different render.",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 128,
    "height": 32,
    "scale": 6,
    "freeze_time": "2026-03-14T23:00:00+00:00",
    "skip_update": true,
    "config": {
      "enabled": true,
      "nhl": {
        "enabled": true
      },
      "ncaa_mens": {
        "enabled": false
      },
      "ncaa_womens": {
        "enabled": false
      }
    }
  },
